WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:05.609
imagine imagine what Eugene sledge that
we talked about tonight

00:00:05.609 --> 00:00:10.050
imagine what he went through on Peleliu
and the tens of thousands of Marines

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:19.949
that suffered that unimaginable horror
and then imagine

00:00:19.949 --> 00:00:24.960
hackworth who he talked about here who
wrote about face assaulting enemy

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:30.599
positions in Korea and he was wounded
over and over again on the line and

00:00:30.599 --> 00:00:42.230
still went back for more and then he got
Alan Seeger the poet who in World War 1

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:50.809
went over the top over and over again to
make his rendezvous with death and

00:00:50.809 --> 00:00:58.739
there's been thousands and hundreds of
thousands and millions of warriors that

00:00:58.739 --> 00:01:06.450
have been in very stressful situations
and faced evil and faced death

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:14.840
much worse than the situation I'm in or
a year in that we might consider

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:19.530
stressful and I even did this when I was
overseas when I was on deployment when I

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:26.460
was a combat leader I was feeling stress
and you know what we took casualties and

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:38.490
it was awful and it was heartbreaking
and but there were other soldiers and

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:44.759
warriors throughout time that had been
in much worse situations Gettysburg or

00:01:44.759 --> 00:01:55.770
vicksburg or the Battle of the Bulge and
in all those horrible situations they

00:01:55.770 --> 00:02:05.250
proved really that humans can withstand
almost most unimaginable stress which

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:14.360
meant to me that I could to and
you can and and the first step for me is

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:23.599
doing that taking that look to gain some
perspective and then in order to gain

00:02:23.599 --> 00:02:26.540
perspective you got to do something that
we already talked about you've got a

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:30.860
detach you've got to detach from the
problems or the stress that you're

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:42.709
experiencing so that you can get that
perspective of them now there's a couple

00:02:42.709 --> 00:02:47.060
different types of stress now if it's
something that you can control that's

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:54.079
causing you stress well why aren't you
getting control of it generally it's a

00:02:54.079 --> 00:03:00.230
lack of discipline so you gotta have the
discipline to grab control and make it

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:02.390
happen
and when I say you need discipline for

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:09.650
that what that means is these stresses
that you're avoiding they're not gonna

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:14.720
go away if you avoid them so take the
discipline to face the stressful

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:22.489
situation and get ahead of it don't be
afraid of it now there's also stress

00:03:22.489 --> 00:03:27.079
that's caused by things that you cannot
control and if you remember talking

00:03:27.079 --> 00:03:33.530
earlier about artillery and how horrible
that was and what made it so horrible

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:40.760
was that there's no control over so if
you can't control something and you

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:50.000
can't get control of it you have to at
least embrace what you can and I'm not

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.440
saying you're gonna embrace artillery
shelling but I'll tell you what when it

00:03:54.440 --> 00:04:01.010
comes to things like artillery or for us
in Ramadi was IEDs and we could do

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:06.650
everything we could do to mitigate that
risk but eventually there's only so much

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:11.959
you can do and you cannot completely
eliminate it but you can't control it so

00:04:11.959 --> 00:04:17.359
why you gonna worry about it why you
gonna stress about it if there's

00:04:17.359 --> 00:04:20.260
something that's completely beyond your
control

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:25.199
you cannot you've got to detach from
and not let yourself get stressed about

00:04:25.199 --> 00:04:33.690
it and on top of that if it's something
that you can't control how can you look

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:37.199
at it in a different light how can you
see it in a way that you could actually

00:04:37.199 --> 00:04:47.159
take advantage of it how can you take
that stress and make it into some kind

00:04:47.159 --> 00:04:53.340
of a lie you know the the chaos of
combat is something that I couldn't

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:56.490
control but I had to embrace it so I
could try and figure out how to take

00:04:56.490 --> 00:05:05.780
advantage of it so when it comes to
stress don't fight it

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:12.240
turn it on itself and use it use it use
it to make yourself sharper and more

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:19.280
alert and use it to make yourself think
more and learn more and get better and

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:29.210
use that stress as a catalyst to make
yourself better

